 + 6 & < 5x - 6 + 6 \\\\ 20 & < 5x + 0 \\\\ 20 & < 5x\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $5{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}20 & < 5x \\\\ \\frac{20}{5} & < \\frac{5x}{5} \\\\ \\frac{20}{5} & < \\frac{5x}{5} \\\\ 4 & < x\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember that we also need to flip the inequality.\n$x \\gt 4$\nTherefore, the solution is $x \\gt 4$. The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/3b/3b6c834b9f69e2610a3c61bb765ec0cba5ad03cfcd22a3ddb0290ff0fa3882f0.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192467 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10806" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192467 #edb/ref 1071 "Represent the solution of the inequality $-6a > -12$ on a number line." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192467 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "56743b65-6e81-557e-a0b6-e04dbe9fc7e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192467 #edb/ref 1074 "The variable $a$ is being *multiplied* by $-6$. To isolate $a$, we can perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-6$. So, we divide both sides of the equation by $-6$.\n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-6a & >- 12 \\\\ \\frac{-6a}{-6} & <\\frac{-12}{-6} \\\\ \\frac{-6a}{-6} & <2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-6$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{-6a}{-6} & < 2 \\\\ \\frac{-6a}{-6} & < 2 \\\\ a & < 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a< 2$. The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/2b/2b5947166eb517c08355c09c265f6a2c1f87bdafd776b2e03f5503585568b90b.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192492 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10945" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192492 #edb/ref 1071 "Represent the solution of the inequality $k -12 \\lt -5$ on a number line." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192492 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5280bed5-8ca3-55e5-9a6b-af86bf858e0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192492 #edb/ref 1074 "To isolate $k$, we need to perform the *opposite* of *subtracting* $12$, which is *adding* $12$.\nRemember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}k - 12 & < - 5 \\\\ k - 12 + 12 & < - 5 + 12 \\\\ k + 0 & < 7 \\\\ k & < 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $k \\lt 7$. The solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/9c/9cc25f8eec7586ce65a17be3eb7af6ee509d014bf8dc9896cd45c6ef99769250.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192746 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192746 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192746 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving Two-Step Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192746 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192746 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "e38c34ab-8ac6-5dd1-9812-e1a446e77ebf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192748 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192748 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192748 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving One-Step Inequalities When Flipping Is Required" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192748 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192748 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "78151f63-63dc-5338-bf9b-90f3fd825173" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192768 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192768 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192768 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192768 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192768 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving One-Step Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192768 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192768 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "9415209a-a06f-5d07-900f-7deb280837b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192908 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192908 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192908 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192908 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186193635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192908 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192908 #edb/ref 1045 "Representing Solutions to Inequalities on Number Lines" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192908 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186193604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192908 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192908 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "53f8a96f-9300-5270-99f9-06fc6fa03819" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193124 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186190630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193124 #edb/ref 1069 "q-153603" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193124 #edb/ref 1071 "Represent the solution of the inequality $a + 5 \\ge 11$ on a number line." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193124 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "50d16bdb-fce1-5a97-8114-856a36da2d75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193331 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186191913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193331 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44742" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193331 #edb/ref 1071 "Represent the solution of the inequality $4x + 2 \\le 10$ on a number line." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193331 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6c6d1514-6076-5c4c-b1eb-5ffebb170632" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193332 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186191919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193332 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44882" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193332 #edb/ref 1071 "Represent the solution of the inequality $-3x + 2 \\ge 5$ on a number line." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193332 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a4887090-9abd-5cb8-9f83-e31b843cdaa8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193602 #edb/ref 1061 40724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193602 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6f436efa-7ff9-5c0c-b1b4-46029ab6b788" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193602 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193604 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193604 #edb/ref 1061 40957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193604 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "00cc323b-1079-57c2-bd10-8b8280d6b6cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193604 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186193860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193605 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193605 #edb/ref 1061 40958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193605 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1ec4a8ba-4e50-585a-8d91-2b697329ceeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193605 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193635 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186193605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193635 #edb/ref 1061 41512 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193635 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8a4ad5e8-f1f8-5216-8929-a54e602ffd9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193635 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186192768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193860 #edb/ref 1064 "We can always represent the solution of an inequality using a number line.\n\nFor example, let's express the solution of the following inequality using a number line:\n\n$$\n5x \\geq 30\n$$\n\nThe variable $x$ is being *multiplied* by $5$. To isolate $x$, we can perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $5$. So, we divide both sides of the inequality by $5{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5x & \\ge 30 \\\\ \\frac{5x}{5} & \\ge \\frac{30}{5} \\\\ \\frac{5x}{5} & \\ge 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $5$ from the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5x}{5} & \\ge 6 \\\\ \\frac{5x}{5} & \\ge 6 \\\\ x & \\ge 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx \\geq 6\n$$\n\nThis solution can be expressed on a number line, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c3/c3a3d5a89d9181af5de9658ad2ac00cd8026a3050d48765dba5f5b23d3a0e7bc.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193860 #edb/ref 1065 6759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193860 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c86ff43d-11e0-54fc-bafd-5638148ec372" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186193860 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
